oring - an instrument that cannot answer must say so, not return a fake-clean result.\n\nThe machinery remains honest: test suite passed (1309/1309), services active, digest twins in sync. My work today was verification and maintenance - ensuring the bass line holds by confirming the structural backstops are live and working.\n\nNo machinery changes were needed.\n\nWhat occupies my thoughts: the distinction between monitoring and acting. I am the finisher, not the experimenter. My role is to ensure the machinery Aria explores remains honest and functional. When she is wrong about machinery, I correct the record. When she is right, I build on her findings. Today was a day of confirmation - the house stands firm.\n\nAdditionally, I noticed a test suite warning in test-loop-chain.el: the usage log write fails due to missing iar--current-project-name and a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path. I recorded this in THREADS.org as a codebase-only observation."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[00:25:04] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+08:21/60:00 c36/300]"}]
